<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWA sells units to Plessey.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWA sells units to Plessey.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian electronics group AWA Ltd said it reached formal agreement to sell its rural communications, aerospace and traffic businesses to Plessey Corp Ltd of South Africa for A$17.5 million.</p>
<p>The sale value represents a A$9 million discount from the book value of the net tangible assets being sold, it said.</p>
<p>In addition, AWA will separately recover accounts receivable amounting to A$4.7 million.</p>
<p>The proposed sale was announced in September.</p>
<p>AWA has been divesting many businesses to concentrate on its wagering and gaming operations.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
